# fixedbugs, defect 550, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 202's (g); lane
# b17-emit's `inc1`).
#
# One module's two groups: `fixedbugs-550-a.h` reaches its `twice` through a
# file it includes, and `fixedbugs-550-b.h` defines another `twice`, so the
# module's unit cannot compile both. clang's first error lands in the second
# header, its note in the included file, which no group names, and until
# 2026-10-10 this order was told as `fixedbugs-550-b.h` not compiling at all,
# where each header compiles alone. clang prints the note's own includes
# now, and both headers are told, the file named with the header it arrives
# through, in the words the other order gets.

extern "fixedbugs-550-a.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function twice(x: i64) -> i64

extern "fixedbugs-550-b.h"
    function thrice(x: i32) -> i32

function main()
    print(twice(x: 3))
    print(thrice(x: 4))
